  "equipment_type": "Air handling / make-up air unit controller (heating, cooling, ventilation)",
  "applies_to": "Engineered Air heating, cooling and ventilation units built with the C-TRAC3 configurable logic controller.",
  "summary": "C-TRAC3 is Engineered Air's configurable unit controller. It supports BACnet MS/TP (9600-76.8k baud) and BACnet IP. The EMS can switch the unit on and off, write the primary and secondary discharge air setpoints and the minimum damper position, start dehumidification and disable the economizer, cooling or heating. It reports temperatures, blower, cooling and heating status, damper position, lockouts, terminal inputs and alarms.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 77077,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The manual gives a descriptive label for each object rather than an Object_Name string; the labels are used as names here.",
    "The discharge setpoint is written to AV 25 (write-only) and read back on AV 26; the secondary setpoint likewise uses AV 27 / AV 28.",
    "Temperatures read in °F or °C, chosen in the SERVICE menu on the PGD1 display.",
    "For the economizer, cooling and heating enables, Off means the function is enabled.",
    "Extra CRD I/O (BI-1 to BI-8, ID-1 to ID-14, Y-1 to Y-4, C-1 to C-13) maps to further AV/BV objects listed by terminal only; their names are on the unit's electrical data sheet, so they are not listed here.",
    "Source: C-TRAC3 Variable Description Table, page 14 (46 objects)."
  ],
